From: Til Kaiser <mail@tk154.de>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: rtl8261n: restore vendor configuration on resume

On some IPQ5332 + RTL8261N setups, the initial link comes up after boot,
but a later netdev down/up cycle leaves the PHY flapping and failing to
re-establish a stable link.

A plain netdev reopen goes through phy_stop()/phy_start(), which suspends
and resumes the PHY. After returning the PHY to normal power state, the
RTL8261N vendor initialization needs to be applied again before link
training restarts.

Restore the vendor configuration from the resume path by calling
rtkphy_config_init() after power-up.

Signed-off-by: Til Kaiser <mail@tk154.de>
---
 drivers/net/phy/rtl8261n/rtk_phy.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/rtl8261n/rtk_phy.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/rtl8261n/rtk_phy.c
@@ -161,11 +161,20 @@ static int rtkphy_c45_suspend(struct phy
 
 static int rtkphy_c45_resume(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
+    int ret;
+
 #ifndef CONFIG_MACH_REALTEK_RTL
-    return rtk_phylib_c45_power_normal(phydev);
-#else
-    return 0;
+    ret = rtk_phylib_c45_power_normal(phydev);
+    if (ret < 0)
+        return ret;
 #endif
+
+    /* Restore the vendor configuration after powering the PHY back up. */
+    ret = rtkphy_config_init(phydev);
+    if (ret < 0)
+        return ret;
+
+    return 0;
 }
 
 static int rtkphy_c45_config_aneg(struct phy_device *phydev)
